.TH SCOTTY 1 "August 2026" "Scotty 0.1.0-beta.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scotty \- send and receive files with nearby devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scotty
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B scotty --send
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Scotty
is a graphical local file-sharing application compatible with Nearby/Quick
Share devices. It uses Bluetooth for discovery and transfers over the local
network, an on-demand Wi-Fi hotspot, or Bluetooth.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user. Later invocations activate the existing
window and forward files to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --send
Open the running instance in send mode with the following local files.
.TP
.B --background
Start without initially showing the main window. This is used by D-Bus and
systemd user-service activation.
.SH BACKGROUND RECEIVING
The packaged service is activated on demand and is not enabled automatically.
To receive continuously after login, run:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user enable --now scotty.service
.fi
.PP
Disable continuous startup with:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user disable --now scotty.service
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/scotty/scotty.log
Default log file when \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR is unset.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/scottydev40/Scotty/issues.
